1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,824
Good morning, Susan.

2
00:00:00,824 --> 00:00:07,427
Good morning, Sam.

3
00:00:07,427 --> 00:00:11,756
What's the schedule today?

4
00:00:11,756 --> 00:00:12,580
Ten o'clock,

5
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,894
telephone FAO Schwarz about the new twin baby dolls.

6
00:00:14,894 --> 00:00:16,085
OK.

7
00:00:16,085 --> 00:00:19,789
Telephone Mrs. Zaskey at the advertising agency.

8
00:00:19,789 --> 00:00:20,921
I did that. Go on.

9
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:23,423
Eleven o'clock, approve the sketches for the toy spaceship.

10
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:24,465
Where are they?

11
00:00:24,465 --> 00:00:26,014
Right here.

12
00:00:26,014 --> 00:00:27,732
Did you look at them?

13
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:29,767
Yes, I did.

14
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:31,991
What do you think of the spaceship?

15
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:34,027
I think the kids'll love it.

16
00:00:34,027 --> 00:00:40,312
Would you show me the drawings, please?

17
00:00:40,312 --> 00:00:45,505
Huh.

18
00:00:45,505 --> 00:00:48,315
Now, what else is on the schedule today?

19
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:49,844
Well, at one o'clock

20
00:00:49,844 --> 00:00:51,860
you have a lunch appointment with Mr. Levine,

21
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:53,776
the client from the Toytown Stores.

22
00:00:53,776 --> 00:00:55,067
Where?

23
00:00:55,067 --> 00:00:56,516
At Rossano's.

24
00:00:56,516 --> 00:00:58,989
Hmm. Anything else?

25
00:00:58,989 --> 00:00:59,952
At four o'clock,

26
00:00:59,952 --> 00:01:01,302
you have a meeting with the production staff

27
00:01:01,302 --> 00:01:02,573
in the conference room.

28
00:01:02,573 --> 00:01:05,105
Make sure everybody is at that meeting.

29
00:01:05,105 --> 00:01:06,356
Will do.

30
00:01:06,356 --> 00:01:09,216
At six you're meeting, Mr. Ozawa.

31
00:01:09,216 --> 00:01:11,440
Oh, yes. Are his models here?

32
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,363
They're in my office.

33
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:13,128
I'd like to see them.

34
00:01:13,128 --> 00:01:14,587
Right.

35
00:01:14,587 --> 00:01:20,793
What else?

36
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:23,166
Come on, Sam ...

37
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:26,016
You work too hard, Susan.

38
00:01:26,016 --> 00:01:28,468
When was your last day off?

39
00:01:28,468 --> 00:01:30,940
Hmm. I can't remember.

40
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:33,433
You really ought to take some time off.

41
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:34,515
What for?

42
00:01:34,515 --> 00:01:38,089
To enjoy the simple things in life ...

43
00:01:38,089 --> 00:01:40,224
I know, Sam.

44
00:01:40,224 --> 00:01:42,061
Maybe soon.

45
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:44,623
To smell the flowers.

46
00:01:44,623 --> 00:01:48,237
Oh, wait a minute. What's today's date?

47
00:01:48,237 --> 00:01:50,679
Today is the twelfth. Why?

48
00:01:50,679 --> 00:01:57,888
It seems to me I scheduled something else.

49
00:01:57,888 --> 00:02:00,718
There's nothing else in the appointment book.

50
00:02:00,718 --> 00:02:02,743
I'm sure I did.

51
00:02:02,743 --> 00:02:06,626
Oh, well, I'll probably remember it later.

52
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,095
I hope it isn't important.

53
00:02:08,095 --> 00:02:10,190
Hmm. It's probably nothing.

54
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,997
OK, let's get started.

55
00:02:11,997 --> 00:02:15,403
Would you call Priscilla Smith at FAO Schwarz, please?

56
00:02:15,403 --> 00:02:22,919
Right.

57
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:25,362
These are the models from the Japanese film maker.

58
00:02:25,362 --> 00:02:30,267
Thank you. Just put them on my desk.

59
00:02:30,267 --> 00:02:34,794
And the new drawings for the toy spaceship.

60
00:02:34,794 --> 00:02:44,604
Wonderful.

61
00:02:44,604 --> 00:02:46,094
That was fast.

62
00:02:46,094 --> 00:02:47,156
We have a new artist.

63
00:02:47,156 --> 00:02:48,675
She's very talented.

64
00:02:48,675 --> 00:02:50,016
What time is it, anyway?

65
00:02:50,016 --> 00:02:50,860
My watch stopped.

66
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:52,647
It's eleven thirty.

67
00:02:52,647 --> 00:02:56,231
What time is my lunch date with Bill Levine?

68
00:02:56,231 --> 00:02:58,187
One o'clock.

69
00:02:58,187 --> 00:03:01,504
Remind me to leave at twelve forty-five.

70
00:03:01,504 --> 00:03:04,155
Did you remember your other appointment for today?

71
00:03:04,155 --> 00:03:05,783
No,

72
00:03:05,783 --> 00:03:07,074
but I have a feeling

73
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:22,017
it's going to be too late when I do remember.

74
00:03:22,017 --> 00:03:23,804
Yes, Sam?

75
00:03:23,804 --> 00:03:26,853
I just solved the mystery.

76
00:03:26,853 --> 00:03:28,084
What did I forget?

77
00:03:28,084 --> 00:03:31,023
You have some guests in the reception room.

78
00:03:31,023 --> 00:03:32,909
What? Who?

79
00:03:32,909 --> 00:03:35,868
Mr. Harry Bennett and his daughter.

80
00:03:35,868 --> 00:03:37,497
I remember!

81
00:03:37,497 --> 00:03:40,048
Oh ... Harry!

82
00:03:40,048 --> 00:03:43,692
I made a lunch date with him and his daughter weeks ago.

83
00:03:43,692 --> 00:03:47,644
Is he a client?

84
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:50,583
He's a friend.

85
00:03:50,583 --> 00:03:54,158
Well, he's here with his daughter to have lunch.

86
00:03:54,158 --> 00:03:55,627
I met her at Thanksgiving,

87
00:03:55,627 --> 00:03:59,847
and I promised to have lunch with both of them today.

88
00:03:59,847 --> 00:04:01,604
Yes, indeed.

89
00:04:01,604 --> 00:04:03,719
What are you going to do about your appointment

90
00:04:03,719 --> 00:04:07,284
with Mr. Levine?

91
00:04:07,284 --> 00:04:12,149
Any suggestions?

92
00:04:12,149 --> 00:04:12,149
Oh!
